    "created_at": "2023-01-23T20:32:00Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-01-23T20:32:00Z",
    "body": "(Procedural note: CSS issues should be filed against [the CSSWG repo](https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/), not HTML's.)\r\n\r\nThe Selectors spec has <https://www.w3.org/TR/selectors-4/#table-pseudos> to address this already - selecting a cell by its column either by index (for your cases, `:nth-col(0)` and `:nth-last-col(0)`) or by matching against a `<col>` element, and these take spans into account. It doesn't address the desire for rows, however. Feel free to open a CSSWG issue for that.\r\n\r\n(That said, despite them existing in the spec, they haven't been implemented yet, due to relatively low author interest.)",
